# 0001. One repo, symlinked into ~, split into numbered conf.d files

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

## Context
The old single `~/.zshrc` grew by hand on two machines (a Mac and an Arch desktop), appended PATH
lines to itself and held credentials. Changes on one machine never reached the other.

## Decision
The config lives in this git repo. `scripts/link.sh` (`make link`) symlinks `zshrc` and the
git/direnv/atuin/lazygit/eza configs into `~`, backing up what was there. `zshrc` only sources
`conf.d/*.zsh` in name order; each file has one job (env, options, plugins, completion, tools,
aliases, functions, devops, local).

## Alternatives
- One big `.zshrc`: hard to find things, merge conflicts between machines.
- A dotfiles manager (chezmoi, stow, yadm): another tool to install for what a 60-line script does.

## Consequences
- `git pull` + `reload` syncs both machines; history and review come for free.
- Load order is the file-name order, so the numbering is part of the contract.
- Editing `~/.zshrc` edits the repo; `.bak-*` files are not the config.

## References
`zshrc`, `scripts/link.sh`, `CLAUDE.md` (map).
